  "id": "distributed-representation",
  "term": "distributed representation",
  "definition": "A distributed representation is a data-driven way of encoding an item as a vector in many dimensions rather than with a single hand-chosen feature. This kind of representation is learned from data so that the resulting features capture useful properties of the item and can improve later analysis or classification.",
